        "original_id": "4472a0d1-8e09-52b9-afd4-237a59dd97fe",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Whitechapel\n- People: Jack the Ripper, Sam Stockman\n- Roles: DC Emerson Kent\n- Places: Whitechapel district of London, United Kingdom\n- Topics: serial killers, copycat murders\n\nFacts:\n- In 1888, Jack the Ripper was active as an unidentified serial killer in and around the impoverished Whitechapel district of London.\n- Sam Stockman was born in 1982 and is a British actor and musician.\n- The first series of Whitechapel was first broadcast in the United Kingdom on 2 February 2009.\n- The first series of Whitechapel depicted a search for a modern copycat killer who replicated the murders of Jack the Ripper.\n- From 2009 to 2013, Sam Stockman played DC Emerson Kent on the UK crime drama Whitechapel.",
